From 595a827d6635ed72cd0b2f215d6f76604d2ba709 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:02:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Record tracked device memory per device for every scene
 device update

Scene::device_update now publishes an immutable record of its tracked
device memory per leaf device when it ends (also on cancel or error):
the update serial, a tag set by the integration (its generation), the
outcome, and per device the exact DeviceInfo id, description and type,
live bytes at the start and end, the highest live bytes during the
update, the largest OptiX build temporary as the driver reports it and as
allocated, the number of builds and how many used the reused temporary or
a local one, and the build temporary still kept at the attributes
boundary. The per-update values are kept apart from the lifetime peak of
Stats, which is unchanged. Scene::get_device_update_memory copies the
record under a lock and never waits for a running update.

Rationale: The memory regression guard for the OptiX build temporaries (0103/0104) needs a whole-update peak per physical GPU and the actual build temporary sizes, which the lifetime peak cannot give.
Contract: Statistics only; scene and device data, allocations and images are unchanged; the existing lifetime memory statistics keep their meaning.
Tests: tests/houdini_device_update_memory_smoke.py
---
